  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 932283,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "Delve into the treacherous depths of Trebor’s castle in *Wizardry: Proving Grounds of the Mad Overlord* for the Commodore 64! This groundbreaking 1981 role-playing game, a pioneer in the Dungeons & Dragons-inspired computer genre, challenges you to create a party of up to six adventurers – choosing from Humans, Elves, Dwarves, Gnomes, and Hobbits – and descend into a sprawling, ten-level dungeon.\n\nCombat is turn-based, and survival demands strategic party management, careful resource allocation, and mastering powerful spells.  Explore a vast, maze-like dungeon, meticulously mapping your progress on graph paper (not included) as you navigate darkness and teleportation traps.  Uncover powerful treasures, gain experience to level up your characters, and confront the evil arch-wizard Werdna.\n\nBe warned: this is a punishing experience!  There are no mid-dungeon saves; a total party wipe means starting over.  The 256K RAM version offers a classic, challenging adventure that defined a generation of RPGs.  Can you conquer the Mad Overlord and retrieve the amulet?"
    },
